    "notes": "Interior species (Zoo 0.84.0). The walker in a country_club_a01 basement, cold run 9052: 'need a lot more species for this room, its just a bunch of chairs and tables with nothing on it'. REFERENCE: a basement or stockroom floor -- kraft cartons with packing tape and the odd shipping label, banker's file boxes with lids and hand holes, stacked in columns, upper cartons set in and turned a few degrees. Geometry planned purely in core/carton_forms.py. BUILT (0.84.0, delco_1997 kit path, unbeveled): 36 tris at 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.3, 132 at 0.9 x 0.6 x 1.0, 1104 at 1.2 x 0.8 x 1.4 (n1), 1824 at 1.6 x 1.2 x 1.8 (n3). BUDGET 2400: the genome's largest stack (two rows of four columns) measured 1968 before bevel over 280 seeded plans; a stockroom holds several, so every box is 12 tris of body and 12 each of tape and label, no bevel."
